{"kind": "mod", "id": 2470, "name": "Keep Starting Gear", "slug": "keep-starting-gear", "teaser": "Auto-saves your gear at raid start. Die? Get it back. Extract? Keep your loot.", "owner_name": "Blackhorse311", "downloads": 9709, "favourites": 12, "featured": false, "contains_ads": false, "contains_ai_content": true, "cheat_notice": false, "license_name": "MIT License", "guid": "blackhorse311.keepstartinggear", "thumbnail_local": null, "category": "Equipment", "category_id": 15, "updated_at": "2026-07-28T08:05:15.000000Z", "created_at": "2025-11-26T04:11:03.000000Z", "published_at": "2026-02-19T20:01:00.000000Z", "latest_constraint": "~4.0.12", "latest_version": "2.0.7", "has_local": false, "has_github": false, "license_link": "https://choosealicense.com/licenses/mit/", "description_html": "<hr />\n<p>Keep Starting Gear</p>\n<p>The cure for gear fear. Protect your loadout. Die without consequences.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>What It Does</p>\n<p>Keep Starting Gear saves your equipment when you enter a raid and restores it if you die. Extract successfully?</p>\n<p>Keep your loot. Die? Get your starting gear back.</p>\n<p>No Run-Through penalty. No exploits. Just protection.</p>\n<p>30 Seconds to Understand</p>\n<p>Enter Raid → Gear auto-saved → Die → Gear restored → Extract → Keep your loot</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Key Features</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Automatic Snapshots – Gear saved at raid start (default) or manually via keybind</li>\n<li>Full Restoration – Durability, ammo counts, medical uses, armor plates, all preserved</li>\n<li>No Penalties – Server-side restoration bypasses “Run-Through” status</li>\n<li>Slot Control – Protect exactly what you want, 16 individual slot toggles</li>\n<li>Modded Items – Works with any custom weapons, armor, and equipment</li>\n<li>SVM Compatible – Works with Server Value Modifier (disable Softcore Mode &amp; Safe Exit)</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>Quick Start</p>\n<p>Extract the archive directly into your SPT root folder (where SPT.Server.exe is located) and merge when prompted.</p>\n<p>Both client and server components are included and pre-configured.</p>\n<p>After install you should have:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Client: BepInEx/plugins/Blackhorse311-KeepStartingGear/Blackhorse311.KeepStartingGear.dll</li>\n<li>Server: SPT/user/mods/Blackhorse311-KeepStartingGear/Blackhorse311.KeepStartingGear.Server.dll</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Default Behavior</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Enter raid – green notification confirms snapshot</li>\n<li>Die – gear automatically restored</li>\n<li>Extract – snapshot cleared, loot kept</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<p>Playstyle Presets</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Casual (Default) – Maximum protection, zero hassle. Auto-snapshot at raid start, all slots protected.</li>\n<li>Hardcore – Manual snapshots only. Exclude Found-in-Raid and insured items. Risk what you find, protect what you bring.</li>\n<li>Custom – Fine-tune every setting: snapshot mode, individual slots, keybinds, notifications.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>Configuration</p>\n<p>Press F12 in-game to access settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Snapshot Mode (Auto Only) – Auto / Auto+Manual / Manual</li>\n<li>Individual Slots (All enabled) – 16 slots individually toggled</li>\n<li>Protect FIR Items (off) – Exclude Found-in-Raid items from snapshots</li>\n<li>Exclude Insured (off) – Let insurance handle insured items</li>\n<li>Manual Keybind (Ctrl+Alt+F8) – Keybind for manual snapshots</li>\n<li>Notifications (on) – On-screen snapshot/restore messages</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>Compatibility</p>\n<ul>\n<li>SPT 4.0.x – Supported, tested on 4.0.12</li>\n<li>SVM – Compatible, disable Softcore Mode &amp; Safe Exit</li>\n<li>FIKA – Not compatible, single-player only</li>\n<li>Custom Items – Full support, works with any modded gear</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>What’s New in v2.0.7</p>\n<p>Critical: Fixed gear not restoring on death when SVM is installed. SVM replaces MatchCallbacks, which prevented our primary restoration path from running. The fallback was too late in SPT’s pipeline. Fix: override SetInventory to restore snapshot items before they get copied to the server profile.</p>\n<p>Medium: Fixed melee weapons being deleted from non-managed Scabbard slots. In normal Tarkov, melee weapons are never lost on death. Scabbard is now always preserved.</p>\n<p>48 unit tests (10 serialization + 38 restoration algorithm). Server-side fix, client DLL unchanged.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Links</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://github.com/Blackhorse311/KeepStartingGear\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">https://github.com/Blackhorse311/KeepStartingGear</a> – Source code, bug reports, documentation</li>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/7ae500007d34edf610e86fcf99a769f6d662b3585c211904b011104d3f691621\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/7ae500007d34edf610e86fcf99a769f6d662b3585c211904b011104d3f691621</a> – 0/64 clean</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Open source. MIT licensed. Community-tested with 40+ bug fixes since v1.0.</p>\n", "versions": [{"version": "1.0.0", "spt_version_constraint": "4.0.6", "content_length": 37086, "downloads": 520, "published_at": "2025-11-26T04:12:00.000000Z", "forge_link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/download/2470/keep-starting-gear/1.0.0", "github_url": null, "external_url": null, "local_path": null, "fika_compatibility": "unknown", "dependencies": []}, {"version": "1.1.0", "spt_version_constraint": "~4.0.7", "content_length": 50888, "downloads": 215, "published_at": "2025-11-30T14:32:00.000000Z", "forge_link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/download/2470/keep-starting-gear/1.1.0", "github_url": null, "external_url": null, "local_path": null, "fika_compatibility": "incompatible", "dependencies": []}, {"version": "1.1.1", "spt_version_constraint": "~4.0.7", "content_length": 48725, "downloads": 295, "published_at": "2025-12-02T06:10:00.000000Z", "forge_link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/download/2470/keep-starting-gear/1.1.1", "github_url": null, "exte